# These workflows are the enforcing half of SpringTree's supply-chain controls:
# a change here changes what every calling repository is allowed to merge. That
# makes them tooling rather than controlled content, so they are owned by the
# same team that owns tooling in the ISMS repository.
#
# A code owner must hold write access to this repository. An entry naming a team
# that does not is not an error — it simply never matches, and the review
# requirement silently does nothing.
#
# This file also has no effect until a ruleset on main requires a review from
# code owners; the organisation baseline requires a pull request but not a
# review.
*  @springtree/isms-tools
